<title>IRAN: NIOC SEES LITTLE MARKET IMPACT FROM IRAQ RETURN.</title>
<headline>NIOC SEES LITTLE MARKET IMPACT FROM IRAQ RETURN.</headline>
<dateline>TEHRAN 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The restart of Iraqi crude exports under the United Nations' &quot;oil-for-food&quot; deal is expected to have little impact on market prices, Iranian Deputy Oil Minister Hojjatollah Ghanimifard said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;A very small change in the price we're going to see,&quot; said Ghanimifard, who is also head of international marketing at National Iranian Oil Company (NIOC).</p>
<p>Iraq resumed lifting oil from the Turkish Mediterranean port of Ceyhan late on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The market had already psychologically taken into account the return of Iraqi oil and consumers would use the resumption of exports to build up their stocks, Ghanimifard said.</p>
</text>
